1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,720
The last video showed the placenta taking charge

2
00:00:02,760 --> 00:00:03,760
of progesterone.

3
00:00:04,240 --> 00:00:06,880
But before a pregnancy, an egg is released

4
00:00:07,040 --> 00:00:08,280
about once a month.

5
00:00:08,560 --> 00:00:11,040
So what stops the ovaries releasing another egg

6
00:00:11,120 --> 00:00:12,000
for nine months?

7
00:00:12,640 --> 00:00:15,040
At the end, why does labour, once it

8
00:00:15,120 --> 00:00:17,120
starts, only get stronger?

9
00:00:17,680 --> 00:00:19,680
And once the baby is born, how does

10
00:00:19,760 --> 00:00:21,600
the body make milk and move it?

11
00:00:22,320 --> 00:00:24,800
Two of the answers are hormone loops, and

12
00:00:24,840 --> 00:00:27,440
the third is two hormone jobs.

13
00:00:28,667 --> 00:00:31,306
Normally, an egg is prepared and released by

14
00:00:31,387 --> 00:00:34,266
hormones from the pituitary, a small gland at

15
00:00:34,347 --> 00:00:35,666
the base of the brain.

16
00:00:36,027 --> 00:00:38,906
FSH makes a follicle, the small sac that

17
00:00:38,987 --> 00:00:40,906
holds an egg, grow.

18
00:00:40,987 --> 00:00:44,186
Then a surge of LH, a sudden rise,

19
00:00:44,307 --> 00:00:46,426
makes the follicle release its egg, which is

20
00:00:46,507 --> 00:00:48,266
called ovulation.

21
00:00:48,347 --> 00:00:51,066
The empty follicle becomes the corpus luteum, which

22
00:00:51,147 --> 00:00:52,346
makes progesterone.

23
00:00:53,567 --> 00:00:56,446
Progesterone travels in the blood to the pituitary,

24
00:00:56,527 --> 00:00:58,926
and it tells the pituitary to release less

25
00:00:59,007 --> 00:01:00,846
FSH and LH.

26
00:01:01,167 --> 00:01:03,966
Progesterone works like a brake on FSH and

27
00:01:04,047 --> 00:01:04,606
LH.

28
00:01:05,167 --> 00:01:08,366
With less FSH and LH, no new follicle

29
00:01:08,407 --> 00:01:10,766
grows, so no egg is released.

30
00:01:11,247 --> 00:01:14,766
That is negative feedback: hormone acts back on

31
00:01:14,847 --> 00:01:17,806
the pituitary, the gland that controls the process,

32
00:01:17,887 --> 00:01:19,726
and turns that process down.

33
00:01:20,934 --> 00:01:22,693
A thermostat works the same way.

34
00:01:23,254 --> 00:01:26,133
The heater warms the room, the thermostat senses

35
00:01:26,214 --> 00:01:28,773
the warmth and switches the heater off.

36
00:01:28,854 --> 00:01:30,933
If the room gets cold, it switches the

37
00:01:30,974 --> 00:01:34,453
heater on, so negative feedback pushes back in

38
00:01:34,534 --> 00:01:34,773
either

39
00:01:35,294 --> 00:01:36,053
direction.

40
00:01:36,294 --> 00:01:39,813
Here, FSH and LH lead to progesterone, and

41
00:01:39,934 --> 00:01:43,253
progesterone turns FSH and LH down.

42
00:01:44,467 --> 00:01:46,946
In a month with no pregnancy, the corpus

43
00:01:46,987 --> 00:01:50,786
luteum breaks down, progesterone falls, the brake comes

44
00:01:50,907 --> 00:01:53,266
off, and the next follicle can grow.

45
00:01:53,587 --> 00:01:56,786
In a pregnancy, hCG keeps the corpus luteum

46
00:01:56,867 --> 00:02:00,146
going, and then the placenta makes the progesterone,

47
00:02:00,227 --> 00:02:03,466
so progesterone stays high for the whole pregnancy.

48
00:02:03,747 --> 00:02:06,066
The source has changed, but the brake works

49
00:02:06,147 --> 00:02:09,266
the same way: the pituitary senses progesterone in

50
00:02:09,307 --> 00:02:12,866
the blood and releases less FSH and LH.

51
00:02:13,107 --> 00:02:15,266
So the brake stays on, and no new

52
00:02:15,347 --> 00:02:16,386
egg is released.

53
00:02:17,600 --> 00:02:20,480
The wall of the uterus is mostly muscle,

54
00:02:20,560 --> 00:02:23,280
and through the pregnancy progesterone helps keep it

55
00:02:23,360 --> 00:02:24,120
calm.

56
00:02:24,480 --> 00:02:27,200
Late in pregnancy, the placenta makes more and

57
00:02:27,280 --> 00:02:29,280
more oestrogen, another hormone.

58
00:02:29,920 --> 00:02:32,480
Oestrogen makes the muscle react more strongly to

59
00:02:32,680 --> 00:02:35,280
oxytocin, the hormone that makes it contract.

60
00:02:35,840 --> 00:02:38,000
So by the end, even a small amount

61
00:02:38,080 --> 00:02:41,040
of oxytocin makes the muscle contract strongly.

62
00:02:42,267 --> 00:02:45,066
Exactly what sets off the first contractions is

63
00:02:45,227 --> 00:02:46,746
still being worked out.

64
00:02:46,827 --> 00:02:49,146
But once they begin, they push the baby's

65
00:02:49,307 --> 00:02:52,106
head down onto the cervix, the narrow lower

66
00:02:52,187 --> 00:02:54,986
end of the uterus, and stretch it.

67
00:02:55,027 --> 00:02:57,786
The stretch sends nerve signals to the brain,

68
00:02:57,827 --> 00:03:01,546
and the pituitary releases oxytocin into the blood.

69
00:03:01,627 --> 00:03:04,506
Oxytocin reaches the uterus muscle, and the muscle

70
00:03:04,587 --> 00:03:05,786
contracts harder.

71
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:09,480
Harder contractions push the baby's head against the

72
00:03:09,640 --> 00:03:13,080
cervix more firmly, so the cervix stretches more,

73
00:03:13,200 --> 00:03:15,320
so more oxytocin is released.

74
00:03:15,640 --> 00:03:18,040
Here the result of the process pushes the

75
00:03:18,120 --> 00:03:20,600
process further, in the same direction.

76
00:03:21,080 --> 00:03:22,760
That is positive feedback.

77
00:03:23,480 --> 00:03:25,720
Nothing in this loop turns it down, so

78
00:03:25,760 --> 00:03:28,520
the contractions build until the baby is born.

79
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:31,800
Then nothing stretches the cervix any more, and

80
00:03:31,880 --> 00:03:33,000
the loop stops.

81
00:03:34,200 --> 00:03:37,360
Negative does not mean bad, and positive does

82
00:03:37,400 --> 00:03:38,440
not mean good.

83
00:03:38,920 --> 00:03:41,720
They describe whether the result opposes the process

84
00:03:41,880 --> 00:03:42,920
or adds to it.

85
00:03:43,560 --> 00:03:46,520
Negative feedback opposes a change, so it keeps

86
00:03:46,600 --> 00:03:47,720
conditions steady.

87
00:03:48,280 --> 00:03:50,840
Positive feedback adds to a change, so it

88
00:03:50,920 --> 00:03:53,000
speeds up until something ends it.

89
00:03:54,200 --> 00:03:55,880
Here is an Explain answer.

90
00:03:56,440 --> 00:03:58,200
First, the negative feedback.

91
00:03:58,760 --> 00:04:01,560
During pregnancy, the corpus luteum and then the

92
00:04:01,600 --> 00:04:03,960
placenta keep progesterone high.

93
00:04:04,440 --> 00:04:08,040
This is negative feedback, because high progesterone reduces

94
00:04:08,120 --> 00:04:11,560
the pituitary's release of FSH and LH, so

95
00:04:11,640 --> 00:04:14,520
no follicles mature and no egg is released.

96
00:04:15,400 --> 00:04:17,320
Second, the positive feedback.

97
00:04:17,720 --> 00:04:20,920
At birth, the baby's head stretches the cervix,

98
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:23,600
which makes the pituitary release oxytocin.

99
00:04:23,880 --> 00:04:27,360
This is positive feedback, because oxytocin strengthens the

100
00:04:27,400 --> 00:04:30,600
contractions, which stretch the cervix more and release

101
00:04:30,760 --> 00:04:31,800
more oxytocin.

102
00:04:32,360 --> 00:04:34,600
It continues until the baby is born, when

103
00:04:34,640 --> 00:04:35,800
the stretch stops.

104
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:39,880
One more hormone job after the birth: feeding

105
00:04:39,960 --> 00:04:40,720
the baby.

106
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:43,520
Prolactin makes the breast produce milk.

107
00:04:43,800 --> 00:04:47,160
Oxytocin makes tiny muscle cells around the milk-making

108
00:04:47,240 --> 00:04:50,200
glands squeeze, which pushes the milk out.

109
00:04:51,400 --> 00:04:54,040
Both are released when the baby suckles, because

110
00:04:54,120 --> 00:04:56,360
nerve signals from the nipple reach the brain

111
00:04:56,600 --> 00:04:58,640
and the pituitary releases them.

112
00:04:59,000 --> 00:05:01,800
Plenty of milk is not made during pregnancy,

113
00:05:01,920 --> 00:05:04,200
because the high progesterone and oestrogen from the

114
00:05:04,280 --> 00:05:06,120
placenta hold it back.

115
00:05:06,440 --> 00:05:08,360
When the placenta leaves the body after the

116
00:05:08,440 --> 00:05:12,280
baby, those levels fall, and milk production begins.

117
00:05:13,500 --> 00:05:14,340
Your turn.

118
00:05:14,540 --> 00:05:15,980
Three situations.

119
00:05:16,300 --> 00:05:19,180
One: a woman who is not pregnant takes

120
00:05:19,220 --> 00:05:21,500
a daily tablet with a hormone that copies

121
00:05:21,580 --> 00:05:24,460
progesterone's action on the pituitary, and it keeps

122
00:05:24,540 --> 00:05:26,220
the level in her blood as high as

123
00:05:26,260 --> 00:05:27,660
in late pregnancy.

124
00:05:28,060 --> 00:05:30,300
What do you predict happens to her FSH

125
00:05:30,380 --> 00:05:33,180
and LH, and to ovulation, the release of

126
00:05:33,220 --> 00:05:34,620
an egg, and why?

127
00:05:35,420 --> 00:05:37,740
Two: a woman is breastfeeding.

128
00:05:38,140 --> 00:05:40,140
Her baby suckles well and her breasts are

129
00:05:40,300 --> 00:05:42,860
making plenty of milk, but very little milk

130
00:05:42,980 --> 00:05:43,860
comes out.

131
00:05:44,220 --> 00:05:46,460
Which hormone's release is more likely to be

132
00:05:46,500 --> 00:05:50,460
the problem, prolactin or oxytocin, and why?

133
00:05:50,860 --> 00:05:55,020
Three: a student writes, "Labour is negative feedback

134
00:05:55,100 --> 00:05:57,660
because it is painful, and the progesterone brake

135
00:05:57,700 --> 00:06:00,700
in pregnancy is positive feedback because it protects

136
00:06:00,740 --> 00:06:03,820
the pregnancy." What is wrong with this, and

137
00:06:03,900 --> 00:06:06,620
which kind of feedback is each, and why?

138
00:06:06,940 --> 00:06:09,020
Pause the video if you'd like more time.

139
00:07:39,434 --> 00:07:42,613
One, LH stays low, so no egg is

140
00:07:42,634 --> 00:07:45,833
released, and FSH is turned down too.

141
00:07:46,154 --> 00:07:49,833
The pituitary senses progesterone, whatever its source, and

142
00:07:49,954 --> 00:07:52,633
turns FSH and LH down.

143
00:07:52,714 --> 00:07:54,953
It is the same brake as in pregnancy,

144
00:07:55,034 --> 00:07:57,086
so it is negative feedback acting on the

145
00:07:57,114 --> 00:07:58,473
pituitary.

146
00:07:58,554 --> 00:08:00,553
If you said she would still ovulate because

147
00:08:00,634 --> 00:08:03,833
she isn't pregnant, remember that the pituitary senses

148
00:08:03,914 --> 00:08:06,633
the hormone, not the pregnancy.

149
00:08:06,714 --> 00:08:09,753
If you said FSH and LH would rise,

150
00:08:09,834 --> 00:08:11,673
check which way the brake pushes.

151
00:08:12,900 --> 00:08:14,580
Two, oxytocin.

152
00:08:14,860 --> 00:08:17,460
Her breasts are making plenty of milk, so

153
00:08:17,540 --> 00:08:19,300
prolactin is working.

154
00:08:19,340 --> 00:08:21,700
The milk is not being squeezed out, so

155
00:08:21,900 --> 00:08:24,740
oxytocin is the more likely problem.

156
00:08:24,820 --> 00:08:26,740
If you said prolactin because it is the

157
00:08:26,820 --> 00:08:30,740
milk hormone, separate making milk from moving milk.

158
00:08:30,780 --> 00:08:34,260
Prolactin makes it, and oxytocin squeezes it out.

159
00:08:35,467 --> 00:08:38,266
Three, the type of feedback depends on whether

160
00:08:38,347 --> 00:08:40,986
the result opposes the process or adds to

161
00:08:41,067 --> 00:08:43,506
it, not on how it feels.

162
00:08:43,947 --> 00:08:47,226
In pregnancy, high progesterone acts on the pituitary

163
00:08:47,307 --> 00:08:50,506
to turn FSH and LH down, the same

164
00:08:50,587 --> 00:08:52,746
brake that works in a normal month, so

165
00:08:52,907 --> 00:08:53,786
it is negative.

166
00:08:54,267 --> 00:08:58,346
In labour, oxytocin strengthens the contractions, which stretch

167
00:08:58,387 --> 00:09:01,626
the cervix more and release more oxytocin, so

168
00:09:01,787 --> 00:09:02,746
it is positive.

169
00:09:03,967 --> 00:09:08,206
Remember, oxytocin squeezes, in the uterus for birth

170
00:09:08,367 --> 00:09:11,006
and in the breast for milk, and prolactin

171
00:09:11,167 --> 00:09:14,246
is pro-lactation, it makes the milk.

172
00:09:14,527 --> 00:09:16,686
And when you see a hormone loop, ask

173
00:09:16,767 --> 00:09:19,486
whether the result opposes the change or adds

174
00:09:19,567 --> 00:09:20,206
to it.

175
00:09:20,527 --> 00:09:22,566
Negative opposes the change.

176
00:09:22,767 --> 00:09:24,406
Positive adds to it.

177
00:09:24,687 --> 00:09:27,326
In these two loops, negative turned the process

178
00:09:27,487 --> 00:09:30,326
down and positive pushed it further.

179
00:09:30,767 --> 00:09:33,966
Next time: how people use reproduction to change

180
00:09:34,047 --> 00:09:35,406
what farms produce.

181
00:09:36,634 --> 00:09:38,073
Here are the key notes.

182
00:09:38,314 --> 00:09:40,233
